* arc-remote-signer\nvalidator key security
** Architecture
*** Host proxy: SignerService :10340
*** Nitro Enclave: EnclaveService on vsock :10350
*** arc-node client over gRPC (tonic)
** Key protection
*** Ed25519 key made with crypto/rand in enclave
*** AES-256-GCM under a KMS data key
*** Data key released only to attested PCR0
*** Ciphertext in Secrets Manager
** Signing path
*** Blind raw-bytes Sign(message)
*** No KMS call on the hot path
*** Plaintext key cached in enclave
left side
** What it does not do
*** No caller authentication, TLS off by default
*** No height/round/step watermark
*** No pubkey pinning or signature check in arc-node
*** Missing secret mints a new key
*** Host picks APP_ENV (log export)
** Compared with
*** CometBFT FilePV: last-sign state
*** tmkms: HSM + SecretConnection + state file
*** Horcrux: threshold Ed25519 + Raft watermark
*** Web3Signer: slashing-protection DB (EIP-3076)
** Hardening
*** mTLS or private network only
*** Double-sign guard in signer or node
*** PCR0 + PCR8 in KMS policy
*** Fail closed on missing secret
@endmindmap
